<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Charles Theodore, Elector of Bavaria</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1724–1799</span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a> · Also known as Karl Theodor</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Charles Theodore was a Wittelsbach prince of the Sulzbach line who inherited the Electoral Palatinate in 1742 and the Electorate of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bavaria">Bavaria</a> in 1777. His attempt to exchange Bavaria for the Austrian <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-the-netherlands">Netherlands</a> led to the War of the Bavarian Succession. A patron of the arts and sciences, he made <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mannheim">Mannheim</a> a musical centre and laid out the English Garden in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/munich">Munich</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/charles-theodore-elector-of-bavaria.jpg" alt="Charles Theodore, Elector of Bavaria" width="320" height="405" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Anna Dorothea Therbusch · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kurf%C3%BCrst_Karl_Theodor_(Bayern).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
